  "tagline": "Embedded, in-process OLAP engine powered by ClickHouse, used mainly from Python.",
  "description": "chDB packages the ClickHouse engine as an in-process library, so a Python (or Go, Rust, Node, C) program can run ClickHouse SQL over Parquet, CSV, Arrow, pandas DataFrames, S3 or remote databases without a server. Sessions can persist tables to a local directory, and newer releases add a pandas-compatible DataStore API. It joined ClickHouse, Inc. in 2024. chDB gives you ClickHouse's function library and formats in a DuckDB-like footprint; it is single-process, the wheel is large, and its non-Python bindings are less mature.",
